               <div draggable="true" data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-dExXmK fNpoDq">
                <p class="sc-kAkozD iOjmJ pf-caret-color-transparent pf-word-wrap-break-word" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Once roasted, coffee begins to lose its flavor the longer it’s exposed to air and moisture. We recommend that you store it in an airtight container in a cool, dark place and grind it just before brewing. Coffee in an unopened FlavorLock bag will stay fresh for several months.</p>
