             <div class="sc-jXbVAB kNtuek pf-r pf-r-eh" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Row" style="--s-xs: 15px; --s-lg: 0px;">
              <div class="pf-c" style="--c-xs: 12; --c-sm: 12; --c-md: 12; --c-lg: 12;">
               <div draggable="true" data-pf-type="Column" class="sc-dExXmK fNpoDq">
                <p class="sc-kAkozD iOjmJ pf-caret-color-transparent pf-word-wrap-break-word" contenteditable="true" spellcheck="false" draggable="true" data-pf-type="Paragraph3">Most people think Espresso Roast has the most caffeine, but brewed coffee is proven to have more. A single 2 oz. Double Espresso shot has about 80 milligrams of caffeine. Whereas an average 12 oz. brewed coffee has about 120 milligrams of caffeine. And our Blast Off Strong Roast formula provides over 1.5x more caffeine than other coffee.</p>
               </div>
              </div>
             </div>
            </div>
           </div>
